1
00:00:04,386 --> 00:00:06,767
The Lives of the Prophets; Part 2

2
00:00:08,032 --> 00:00:11,906
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:12,952 --> 00:00:16,222
Before I go to the next section of the story of Musa(موسى);

4
00:00:16,482 --> 00:00:19,169
Let's look at the story of Musa(موسى) up to this point.

5
00:00:19,615 --> 00:00:25,903
Until now, up to this point, Musa(موسى) is not a prophet yet; He's not the messenger.

6
00:00:27,517 --> 00:00:37,455
So, why is Allahسُبحانه وتعالى telling us all of this history record of the life of Musa(موسى) before Risaalah(رسالة), before the message-hood or prophet-hood?

7
00:00:38,248 --> 00:00:43,711
You know, it's very important for us to know this background of Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى).

8
00:00:44,582 --> 00:00:54,365
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is putting Musa(موسى) through experiences that he will need in his mission, as a messenger.

9
00:00:54,618 --> 00:01:00,024
First of all, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى raised up Musa(موسى) in the palace of Firaun(فرعون).

10
00:01:00,618 --> 00:01:06,151
So that Musa(موسى) can be an insider; He sees how the government functions from the inside.

11
00:01:06,498 --> 00:01:09,511
So he has expertise; He knows what's happening.

12
00:01:09,541 --> 00:01:10,771
Just like, what happened with Yusuf(يوسُف)?

13
00:01:10,801 --> 00:01:11,584
Where was he raised?

14
00:01:11,804 --> 00:01:15,431
He was raised in the house of the prime minister or the treasure.

15
00:01:15,891 --> 00:01:19,620
So he has knowledge of how the governments functions and works.

16
00:01:19,933 --> 00:01:27,282
Also, Musa(موسى) has first-hand knowledge of the corruption of Firaun(فرعون), because he has seen it with his own eyes.

17
00:01:28,422 --> 00:01:31,728
And look at the travelling of Musa(موسى).

18
00:01:32,015 --> 00:01:35,252
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made Musa(موسى) travel out of Egypt.

19
00:01:35,685 --> 00:01:37,665
And we know that Al-Imaam-Al-Shaafi(امام الشافى) says;

20
00:01:37,805 --> 00:01:44,510
تَغَرَّب عَنِ الأَوطانِ في طَلَبِ العُلا وَسافِر فَفي الأَسفارِ خَمسُ فَوائِدِ

21
00:01:45,024 --> 00:01:53,055
 تَفَرُّجُ هَمٍّ وَاِكتِسابُ مَعيشَةٍ وَعِلمٌ وَآدابٌ وَصُحبَةُ ماجِدِ

22
00:01:53,454 --> 00:01:59,733
Imaam-Al-Shaafi(امام الشافى) says; Leave your country in search of exaltation

23
00:02:00,018 --> 00:02:03,238
and travel because there are five benefits in traveling;

24
00:02:03,799 --> 00:02:05,459
To relief your despair,

25
00:02:05,659 --> 00:02:07,286
to seek a livelihood,

26
00:02:07,652 --> 00:02:08,892
to seek knowledge,

27
00:02:09,119 --> 00:02:12,432
to seek manners and new behaviors,

28
00:02:13,230 --> 00:02:18,337
and finally he said; to be accompanying somebody who is righteous.

29
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:21,526
These are benefits that you could get through traveling.

30
00:02:22,006 --> 00:02:27,186
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) travel in the land so that, he can learn.

31
00:02:28,019 --> 00:02:29,119
Number three;

32
00:02:29,573 --> 00:02:35,500
What type of job did Musa(موسى) serve, when he was working with this man?

33
00:02:36,233 --> 00:02:37,353
راعي الغنم

34
00:02:37,606 --> 00:02:39,660
A shepherd of goat or sheep.

35
00:02:40,046 --> 00:02:41,450
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

36
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:43,267
ما من نبي الا ورعى الغنم

37
00:02:43,446 --> 00:02:46,599
Every prophet has been a shepherd of sheep.

38
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:50,352
Why specifically sheep and why specifically a shepherd?

39
00:02:52,058 --> 00:02:55,745
Being a shepherd is being responsible.

40
00:02:56,798 --> 00:02:58,502
And being a shepherd of sheep. ?

41
00:02:58,836 --> 00:03:02,662
Sheep are the weakest of the livestock that we have.

42
00:03:03,069 --> 00:03:05,976
It is weaker than cows and it's weaker than camels.

43
00:03:06,242 --> 00:03:10,219
And that weakness makes the shepherd very alert.

44
00:03:10,393 --> 00:03:17,438
He has to have his eyes always open to take care and guard these sheep from a wolf;

45
00:03:17,851 --> 00:03:20,651
to take care of them of being lost.

46
00:03:20,901 --> 00:03:24,804
Because the sheep cannot survive on its own but the camel can.

47
00:03:25,804 --> 00:03:28,417
So, the shepherd learns how to be very alert.

48
00:03:28,544 --> 00:03:35,182
Because the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) are going to be protecting a whole nation; a whole nation of weak people.

49
00:03:35,232 --> 00:03:35,793
Because;

50
00:03:35,907 --> 00:03:37,248
خُلِقَ الْإِنْسَانُ ضَعِيفًا۝

51
00:03:37,556 --> 00:03:39,647
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; the human being is weak.

52
00:03:40,567 --> 00:03:45,147
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى makes them go through this training; of being shepherds.

53
00:03:45,347 --> 00:03:47,220
So that, they learn; how to be responsible.

54
00:03:47,546 --> 00:03:51,353
Because it's the responsibility of the shepherd to take care of the flock.

55
00:03:54,384 --> 00:03:57,064
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى was preparing Musa(موسى) for what?

56
00:03:57,484 --> 00:04:03,288
Allah was preparing him for the most difficult job of all.

57
00:04:03,548 --> 00:04:07,308
The most difficult job of all is the job of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

58
00:04:07,881 --> 00:04:12,545
That's the most difficult work; It is the work of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

59
00:04:12,575 --> 00:04:20,684
And the particular work of Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) was going to be one of the most challenging work that any Nabi(نَبِي) has faced.

60
00:04:20,931 --> 00:04:23,331
Because, who is Musa(موسى) going to be dealing with?

61
00:04:23,437 --> 00:04:25,811
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is sending him to Firaun(فرعون).

62
00:04:26,364 --> 00:04:28,958
Allah is sending him to the man; who claimed to be God.

63
00:04:28,988 --> 00:04:30,356
أَنَا۠ رَبُّكُمُ ٱلْأَعْلَى۝

64
00:04:30,618 --> 00:04:32,657
وَمَا عَلِمْتُ لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرِي

65
00:04:32,974 --> 00:04:41,782
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is sending Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) to face the oldest monarchy living on the face of the earth and that is the family of Firaun(فرعون).

66
00:04:41,895 --> 00:04:46,102
This family who believed that divine blood is running through their veins.

67
00:04:46,315 --> 00:04:50,002
They believe that they are the seeds of God; that they are the children of God.

68
00:04:50,455 --> 00:04:55,269
This family that rule over an empire of the rich Nile River.

69
00:04:55,442 --> 00:04:59,595
They have been ruling for centuries and centuries and nobody dares to stand against them.

70
00:04:59,781 --> 00:05:05,648
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is going to send one man against this strong, powerful family headed by Firaun(فرعون).

71
00:05:07,221 --> 00:05:10,497
A superpower or an empire or civilization of his time.

72
00:05:11,330 --> 00:05:12,225
That's on one hand.

73
00:05:12,645 --> 00:05:17,640
On the other hand; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is sending Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) to deal with Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل);

74
00:05:17,853 --> 00:05:22,100
A nation that has some remnants of the religion of Allah.

75
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:28,554
But it has been mixed with so much culture and tradition, that it has a different face.

76
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:33,950
And they have been living under oppression for a very long time.

77
00:05:34,624 --> 00:05:38,984
And that oppression has eroded the dignity that they have.

78
00:05:39,444 --> 00:05:42,498
And it has caused their personalities to be humiliated.

79
00:05:42,785 --> 00:05:46,852
And that is what happens to people when they live under oppression for a long time.

80
00:05:47,472 --> 00:05:52,122
And we found that in the story of Musa(موسى) and the two men who are fighting;

81
00:05:52,152 --> 00:05:55,795
one of them was from children of Israel and one of them was from the Egyptians.

82
00:05:56,175 --> 00:06:00,198
When Musa(موسى) came to interfere, what did the Bani Israeli(بني أسرائيلى) say?

83
00:06:00,631 --> 00:06:04,104
He said; You want to kill me like you have killed somebody the day before.

84
00:06:04,278 --> 00:06:07,176
So, he betrayed Musa(موسى), who helped him the day before.

85
00:06:07,429 --> 00:06:12,154
So, you find that the people who live under oppression for a very long time; they become very selfish.

86
00:06:12,528 --> 00:06:15,521
Because the government makes sure that they are divided.

87
00:06:15,628 --> 00:06:18,001
Because if they're united; the government will not survive.

88
00:06:18,274 --> 00:06:19,619
So, they divide the people.

89
00:06:19,805 --> 00:06:21,779
They plant the seeds of division among them.

90
00:06:21,972 --> 00:06:24,092
So, then you have people who are living in their own islands.

91
00:06:24,159 --> 00:06:27,359
They are thinking individualistically in a selfish way.

92
00:06:28,092 --> 00:06:30,572
These are the kind of people that Musa(موسى) is going to deal with.

93
00:06:30,759 --> 00:06:32,412
A kind of people who lost dignity.

94
00:06:32,442 --> 00:06:33,851
اذْهَبْ أَنتَ وَرَبُّكَ فَقَاتِلَا

95
00:06:33,988 --> 00:06:36,144
Go and fight with your Lord, we're going to sit right here.

96
00:06:36,877 --> 00:06:43,897
So, this was the mission; the difficult mission, that Syedina Musa(عليه الصلوة والسلام) was going to be faced with.

97
00:06:45,003 --> 00:06:51,123
But until now, Musa(موسى) has no idea, what Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is hiding for him in the future?

98
00:06:51,617 --> 00:06:58,274
Musa(موسى) has been away from his mother and his family and his country for 10 years.

99
00:06:58,841 --> 00:07:01,213
He feels homesick; He misses his family.

100
00:07:02,140 --> 00:07:06,400
He wants to go back and visit his mother; He wants to visit his family.

101
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:12,800
So, he decided that he's going to go to Egypt; Secretly, he will sneak in, without the government knowing

102
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:16,573
and go and meet with his family and relatives.

103
00:07:17,725 --> 00:07:22,878
So, he took with him his wife and he started traveling towards Egypt.

104
00:07:23,392 --> 00:07:26,580
Musa(موسى) got lost; He lost the directions.

105
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:29,533
It was a very cold and dark night.

106
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:33,700
And Musa(موسى) is traveling in this cold and dark night.

107
00:07:34,067 --> 00:07:40,654
He lost direction; There is no light; It was completely dark and it was very cold.

108
00:07:41,254 --> 00:07:46,555
And Musa(موسى) is with his wife; alone, in this very difficult environment; its desert.

109
00:07:46,869 --> 00:07:50,902
That area which is between Ash-Sham(ألشَّام)  and Egypt, is desert.

110
00:07:51,375 --> 00:07:56,241
Musa(موسى) saw; what appeared to be fire far away.

111
00:07:57,248 --> 00:08:01,722
And it seems from the Ayaat(آيات); that only Musa(موسى) was able to see it but his wife didn't see it.

112
00:08:01,752 --> 00:08:02,873
إِنِّي آنَسْتُ نَارًا

113
00:08:02,903 --> 00:08:04,009
I have seen light.

114
00:08:04,296 --> 00:08:09,712
It seems that this light; because it was a special light only Musa(موسى) was seeing it; his wife couldn't recognize it.

115
00:08:10,949 --> 00:08:12,246
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

116
00:08:12,406 --> 00:08:22,159
فَلَمَّا قَضَىٰ مُوسَى الْأَجَلَ وَسَارَ بِأَهْلِهِ آنَسَ مِن جَانِبِ الطُّورِ نَارًا۝

117
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:24,326
And, he was traveling with his family.

118
00:08:24,356 --> 00:08:26,913
He saw a fire in the direction of At-Toor(الطور).

119
00:08:27,599 --> 00:08:37,581
He told his wife; wait here, I will go and either try to find directions.

120
00:08:38,281 --> 00:08:43,767
Because, that fire must be burned by some people; there must be some people around it.

121
00:08:43,927 --> 00:08:46,014
So, they'll give me directions; I need guidance.

122
00:08:46,121 --> 00:08:47,128
Musa(موسى) needs guidance.

123
00:08:47,175 --> 00:08:47,751
He says;

124
00:08:47,908 --> 00:08:49,589
لَعَلِّيْ أَجِدُ عَلَى النَّارِ هُدًى۝

125
00:08:49,823 --> 00:08:51,743
That I will find guidance next to the fire.

126
00:08:51,773 --> 00:08:53,056
What guidance is he talking about?

127
00:08:53,329 --> 00:08:54,396
Directions to Egypt.

128
00:08:54,876 --> 00:09:03,336
لَّعَلِّیْۤ اٰتِیْكُمْ مِّنْهَا بِقَبَسٍ اَوْ اَجِدُ عَلَى النَّارِ هُدًى۝

129
00:09:03,390 --> 00:09:09,047
So that I could either bring you some light because we need light; we are in complete darkness

130
00:09:09,594 --> 00:09:11,534
or I will find the guidance.

131
00:09:12,387 --> 00:09:16,362
لَّعَلِّیْۤ اٰتِیْكُمْ مِّنْهَا بِقَبَسٍ اَوْ اَجِدُ عَلَى النَّارِ هُدًى۝

132
00:09:17,186 --> 00:09:18,982
So, Musa(موسى) walked to that direction.

133
00:09:19,375 --> 00:09:21,682
Musa(موسى) doesn't know, what he's going to face in front of him?

134
00:09:23,015 --> 00:09:33,656
He walks there and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى tells us about one of the most amazing conversations that happened in the history of the universe.

135
00:09:34,396 --> 00:09:35,656
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

136
00:09:35,686 --> 00:09:46,043
فَلَمَّآ أَتَىٰهَا نُودِىَ مِن شَٰطِئِ ٱلْوَادِ ٱلْأَيْمَنِ فِى ٱلْبُقْعَةِ ٱلْمُبَٰرَكَةِ مِنَ ٱلشَّجَرَةِ

137
00:09:46,439 --> 00:09:54,303
أَن يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِنِّىٓ أَنَا ٱللَّهُ رَبُّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ۝

138
00:09:54,713 --> 00:09:56,143
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

139
00:09:56,296 --> 00:09:58,373
So when he reached the fire.

140
00:09:58,633 --> 00:10:04,413
He was called from the right side of the valley, in the blessed place from the tree.

141
00:10:04,599 --> 00:10:09,923
Oh Musa(موسى)! Verily, I am Allah; the Lord of Al-Alameen(العالمين).

142
00:10:10,649 --> 00:10:12,796
And then, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى);

143
00:10:13,023 --> 00:10:19,229
اِنِّیْۤ اَنَا رَبُّكَ فَاخْلَعْ نَعْلَیْكَۚ-

144
00:10:19,595 --> 00:10:24,611
اِنَّكَ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًى۝

145
00:10:24,681 --> 00:10:28,658
Oh Musa(موسى)! Take off your shoes because you are in the Sacred Valley.

146
00:10:29,505 --> 00:10:33,435
You have to come into this meeting with preparation; take off your shoes.

147
00:10:33,842 --> 00:10:35,895
Just like, we enter into Salah(صلاة) with Wudhu(وضو).

148
00:10:36,155 --> 00:10:39,328
So he went in, to that sacred valley; in At-Toor(الطور).

149
00:10:39,842 --> 00:10:43,115
And then he saw this tree; green tree.

150
00:10:43,535 --> 00:10:48,435
There was fire burning in it but the tree is becoming more green and green.

151
00:10:49,562 --> 00:10:52,088
And that fire was not fire but it was light.

152
00:10:52,282 --> 00:10:56,068
And then he watched and he saw that light was extending up to the Samawat(سماوات).

153
00:10:56,568 --> 00:10:58,774
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told him;

154
00:10:58,804 --> 00:11:02,328
اِنَّنِیْۤ اَنَا اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنَا

155
00:11:02,695 --> 00:11:05,444
I am Allah, there's no God but Me.

156
00:11:05,664 --> 00:11:10,550
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى spoke to Musa(موسى) in those special moments.

157
00:11:11,550 --> 00:11:14,151
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى);

158
00:11:14,418 --> 00:11:27,600
اِنَّنِیْۤ اَنَا اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنَا فَاعْبُدْنِیْۙ-وَ اَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ لِذِكْرِیْ۝

159
00:11:28,230 --> 00:11:34,737
There's no god but Me; So, worship me and establish prayer for My remembrance.

160
00:11:35,564 --> 00:11:37,291
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told him;

161
00:11:37,321 --> 00:11:41,801
إِنَّ السَّاعَةَ آتِيَةٌ أَكَادُ أُخْفِيهَا لِتُجْزَى كُلُّ نَفْسٍ بِمَا تَسْعَى۝

162
00:11:41,961 --> 00:11:46,761
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى) about the hour; the day of Judgment; Al-Akhira(الآخرة).

163
00:11:47,652 --> 00:11:49,435
Now let's go back a little bit.

164
00:11:50,615 --> 00:11:54,081
Musa(موسى), what did he want from this fire?

165
00:11:54,874 --> 00:11:56,134
He wanted two things.

166
00:11:57,061 --> 00:12:06,433
He wanted light; to light up the small area which he and his wife and his sheep are sitting in

167
00:12:07,447 --> 00:12:09,434
but he came back with light for humanity.

168
00:12:11,114 --> 00:12:14,242
Musa(موسى) went to that fire because he wants guidance,

169
00:12:14,755 --> 00:12:19,967
so that someone will tell him the direction to Egypt but he came back for guidance for mankind.

170
00:12:22,001 --> 00:12:23,480
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told him;

171
00:12:23,510 --> 00:12:26,596
إِنَّنِىٓ أَنَا ٱللَّهُ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنَا۠ فَٱعْبُدْنِى

172
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:28,686
I am Allah so worship Me;

173
00:12:28,769 --> 00:12:29,831
Tawheed(تؤحيد); Number one;

174
00:12:30,223 --> 00:12:35,556
Oneness of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and what was the next order after Tawheed(تؤحيد)?

175
00:12:36,043 --> 00:12:38,093
أَقِمِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ لِذِكْرِىٓ۝

176
00:12:38,123 --> 00:12:40,127
Established prayer for my remembrance.

177
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:46,134
Salah(صلاة) was prescribed on Musa(موسى) in a direct conversation between him and Allah.

178
00:12:46,687 --> 00:12:50,365
And how was Salah(صلاة) prescribed on Muhammadﷺ.?

179
00:12:50,745 --> 00:12:55,472
It was prescribed on him in the trip of Al-Mairaj(المعراج) without anyone in between.

180
00:12:56,519 --> 00:12:58,179
That is the importance of Salah(صلاة).

181
00:12:58,646 --> 00:13:01,703
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told him, what He has told every prophet?

182
00:13:01,763 --> 00:13:05,325
And that is the people need to believe in the Akhira(آخرة); in the afterlife.

183
00:13:06,525 --> 00:13:07,785
السَّاعَةَ آتِيَةٌ

184
00:13:08,078 --> 00:13:09,383
The hour will come.

185
00:13:09,543 --> 00:13:10,723
أَكَادُ أُخْفِيهَا

186
00:13:10,836 --> 00:13:16,930
I am hiding it; It's so close; If it is there, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى just hiding it away from the people.

187
00:13:18,903 --> 00:13:24,790
In this wonderful conversation between the creator and the servant; Musa عليه السلام.

188
00:13:26,183 --> 00:13:27,650
Musa(موسى) is holding his stick.

189
00:13:28,490 --> 00:13:32,416
He's holding his stick which he has lived with for a very long time. He knows his stick very well.

190
00:13:32,446 --> 00:13:34,069
Musa(موسى) knows his stick very well.

191
00:13:35,674 --> 00:13:38,766
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى asks him about his stick.

192
00:13:40,366 --> 00:13:42,639
وَمَا تِلْكَ بِيَمِينِكَ يَا مُوسَى۝

193
00:13:44,071 --> 00:13:48,339
What is that in your hands, Oh Musa(موسى)?

194
00:13:49,292 --> 00:13:50,779
What is in your right hand?

195
00:13:51,212 --> 00:13:54,293
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants him to say; what he knows about his stick.

196
00:13:54,660 --> 00:13:56,960
Because Allah wants to show him, what he doesn't know.

197
00:13:57,980 --> 00:14:00,812
So, Musa(موسى) told Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

198
00:14:00,992 --> 00:14:06,135
according to his knowledge, what he knows about this stick which he has owned for a very long time.

199
00:14:06,515 --> 00:14:07,028
He said;

200
00:14:07,108 --> 00:14:11,942
قَالَ هِيَ عَصَايَ أَتَوَكَّأُ عَلَيْهَا وَأَهُشُّ بِهَا عَلَى غَنَمِي وَلِيَ فِيهَا مَآرِبُ أُخْرَى۝

201
00:14:12,136 --> 00:14:23,001
He said; This is my stick, where on I lean and where with I beat down branches for my sheep and where in I find other uses.

202
00:14:23,716 --> 00:14:25,989
I use it to lean on when I need to climb

203
00:14:26,542 --> 00:14:31,343
and I use it to beat down branches and leaves to feed my sheep.

204
00:14:31,787 --> 00:14:33,887
And I also use it for other things.

205
00:14:34,587 --> 00:14:36,160
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى);

206
00:14:36,313 --> 00:14:37,454
أَلْقِهَا يَا مُوسَى۝

207
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:38,659
Throw it.

208
00:14:40,007 --> 00:14:44,355
So Musa(موسى) threw away his stick and what happened?

209
00:14:44,569 --> 00:14:46,016
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

210
00:14:46,046 --> 00:14:48,222
وَأَنْ أَلْقِ عَصَاكَ ۖ

211
00:14:48,555 --> 00:14:59,412
فَلَمَّا رَءَاهَا تَهْتَزُّ كَأَنَّهَا جَآنٌّ وَلَّىٰ مُدْبِرًا وَلَمْ يُعَقِّبْ ۚ

212
00:14:59,548 --> 00:15:05,482
So, he threw his stick from his hand and it started to shake.

213
00:15:06,762 --> 00:15:11,519
The stick is dead but Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is the One Who created life and death.

214
00:15:12,792 --> 00:15:17,826
So that stick that is dead; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put in it, a soul of a snake.

215
00:15:18,899 --> 00:15:24,217
For Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, it is exactly as creating anything else.

216
00:15:24,297 --> 00:15:26,520
For Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; it is Kun-Fayakun(كُنْ فَيَكُونُ).

217
00:15:27,547 --> 00:15:31,207
But this is unusual for Musa(موسى) who knows his stick for a very long time.

218
00:15:31,674 --> 00:15:32,619
So when Musa(موسى);

219
00:15:32,679 --> 00:15:35,020
 رَءَاهَا تَهْتَزُّ كَأَنَّهَا جَآنٌّ

220
00:15:35,167 --> 00:15:37,974
It started shaking like a huge serpent.

221
00:15:39,535 --> 00:15:42,168
Musa(موسى); what was his first reaction?

222
00:15:42,708 --> 00:15:44,895
It was a reaction of a human being.

223
00:15:45,188 --> 00:15:47,743
فَوَلَّىٰ مُدْبِرًا وَلَمْ يُعَقِّبْ ۚ

224
00:15:48,097 --> 00:15:52,107
He ran away and he did not look back; He ran away;

225
00:15:52,137 --> 00:15:54,336
فَوَلَّىٰ مُدْبِرًا وَلَمْ يُعَقِّبْ ۚ

226
00:15:54,366 --> 00:15:55,467
He didn't even look back.

227
00:15:56,177 --> 00:16:00,654
Because this is a stick which he knew for a very long time and now suddenly, it's a huge Snake.

228
00:16:01,727 --> 00:16:03,374
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is training Musa(موسى).

229
00:16:03,608 --> 00:16:06,877
This natural human fear has to get out of his heart.

230
00:16:07,789 --> 00:16:11,957
This is natural; It is a natural human trait to have fear in your heart.

231
00:16:12,384 --> 00:16:18,180
But Musa(موسى) is going to be dealing with situations and he has to have a strong heart.

232
00:16:18,210 --> 00:16:20,076
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is preparing him for that.

233
00:16:20,106 --> 00:16:21,367
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى);

234
00:16:21,397 --> 00:16:24,046
يَا مُوسَىٰ أَقْبِلْ وَلَا تَخَفْ ۖ إِنَّكَ مِنَ الْآمِنِينَ۝

235
00:16:24,595 --> 00:16:30,520
Oh Musa(موسى)! come here and do not have any fear because you are going to be safe and secure.

236
00:16:32,342 --> 00:16:33,612
So Musa(موسى) came back.

237
00:16:34,379 --> 00:16:36,078
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told him;

238
00:16:36,692 --> 00:16:38,538
وَاضْمُمْ يَدَكَ إِلَىٰ جَنَاحِكَ

239
00:16:38,758 --> 00:16:41,598
Put your right hand under your arm.

240
00:16:42,512 --> 00:16:45,260
Musa(موسى) was dark skinned, as we said.

241
00:16:46,007 --> 00:16:49,940
He pulled out his hand it was white and shining like the moon.

242
00:16:50,947 --> 00:16:55,243
Allah told them to put his hand back; He put his hand back; it returned to it's natural colour.

243
00:16:56,451 --> 00:16:57,271
Two signs;

244
00:16:57,424 --> 00:16:58,893
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

245
00:16:59,286 --> 00:17:01,280
لنريك من اياتنا الكبرى۝

246
00:17:01,345 --> 00:17:03,692
That we may show you, some of our greater signs.

247
00:17:04,346 --> 00:17:09,422
These are two, out of nine signs; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given Musa(موسى) and we'll talk about the other signs later.

248
00:17:10,622 --> 00:17:12,689
Now, hold your breath for the next thing.

249
00:17:13,542 --> 00:17:16,534
This is a short conversation between Allah and Musa(موسى).

250
00:17:17,081 --> 00:17:20,534
Musa(موسى) is just confronted with the responsibility.

251
00:17:20,974 --> 00:17:26,770
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is handing down Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى); the responsibility of Prophet-hood.

252
00:17:27,623 --> 00:17:31,123
But what was the first command that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given Musa(موسى)?

253
00:17:33,110 --> 00:17:34,866
اِذْهَبْ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ

254
00:17:35,506 --> 00:17:37,414
Go to Firaun(فرعون), immediately.

255
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:41,367
Musa(موسى) just received the message right now.

256
00:17:42,461 --> 00:17:45,030
And in this conversation between him Allah;

257
00:17:45,217 --> 00:17:50,640
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is already handing him; the challenging mission of going and facing Firaun(فرعون).

258
00:17:50,713 --> 00:17:53,189
اِذْهَبْ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّهٗ طَغٰى۝

259
00:17:53,370 --> 00:17:56,167
Go to Firaun(فرعون) because he has transgressed all bounds.

260
00:17:56,767 --> 00:17:59,289
This is a very, very heavy order.

261
00:17:59,942 --> 00:18:00,802
قَوْلًا ثَقِيلً

262
00:18:00,832 --> 00:18:01,589
This is heavy.

263
00:18:02,449 --> 00:18:06,575
Musa(موسى) ran out of Egypt for 10 years because of fear of Firaun(فرعون).

264
00:18:06,635 --> 00:18:11,350
He wants to visit his family and his mother and his relatives and his home country.

265
00:18:11,650 --> 00:18:14,137
He's not going there because of the fear of Firaun(فرعون).

266
00:18:14,697 --> 00:18:20,579
And now, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is telling him not to go into Egypt; to go to Firaun(فرعون) and tell him to follow you.

267
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:31,488
But Musa عليه السلام; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى chose him because of his strength and his Eeman(ايمان).

268
00:18:31,855 --> 00:18:33,038
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

269
00:18:33,378 --> 00:18:34,178
يَجْتَبِي

270
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:37,098
He chooses out of his creation, the best for this mission of Prophet-hood.

271
00:18:37,405 --> 00:18:41,767
So Musa(موسى) did not reject the command of Allah.

272
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:44,087
But he asked Allah for help.

273
00:18:44,713 --> 00:18:46,893
Because this is not an easy thing to do.

274
00:18:47,667 --> 00:18:49,561
So, he told Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

275
00:18:49,808 --> 00:18:51,241
قَالَ رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِي صَدْرِي۝

276
00:18:51,271 --> 00:18:55,061
Notice and look at this wonderful Dua(دُعَا) of Musa(موسى), what he's asking from Allah?

277
00:18:55,334 --> 00:18:56,006
Number one;

278
00:18:56,168 --> 00:18:59,250
قَالَ رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِي صَدْرِي۝

279
00:18:59,355 --> 00:19:03,630
Oh Allah! Open up; my heart and my chest.

280
00:19:04,343 --> 00:19:09,652
Open for me my chest; Grant me self confidence and contentment and boldness.

281
00:19:09,985 --> 00:19:13,512
This mission of facing Firaun(فرعون), needs to have a very strong heart.

282
00:19:13,542 --> 00:19:18,203
So, open for me my heart, give me strength, give me confidence.

283
00:19:18,996 --> 00:19:22,496
وَيَسِّرْ لِي أَمْرِي۝

284
00:19:22,609 --> 00:19:24,639
And make my mission easy.

285
00:19:25,079 --> 00:19:27,519
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى can make the difficult easy.

286
00:19:28,039 --> 00:19:31,939
وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِّن لِّسَانِي۝

287
00:19:32,079 --> 00:19:36,237
And make loose the knot; the defect from my tongue.

288
00:19:36,957 --> 00:19:38,987
Musa(موسى) had a problem with speech.

289
00:19:39,047 --> 00:19:44,876
We do not know what exactly there's that story of the charcoal and all that but there's no evidence for it.

290
00:19:44,906 --> 00:19:51,055
Anyway, we know from the Nas(نص) of Qur'an; from the text of Qur'an that Musa(موسى) had the problem with the way, he used to speak.

291
00:19:51,475 --> 00:19:53,679
 Either, it was difficulty in pronouncing letters

292
00:19:53,846 --> 00:19:55,957
or it was difficulty in expressing himself

293
00:19:56,166 --> 00:19:59,136
or difficultly in he was tattering, AllahuAalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ).

294
00:19:59,357 --> 00:20:03,217
But he had certain defect in the way he used to speak.

295
00:20:03,484 --> 00:20:05,013
So, he asked Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

296
00:20:05,043 --> 00:20:06,320
وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِّن لِّسَانِي۝

297
00:20:06,478 --> 00:20:08,630
And release one of the knots from my tongue.

298
00:20:08,836 --> 00:20:10,913
He didn't ask Allah to make him the most fluent;

299
00:20:11,060 --> 00:20:15,647
He asked Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to release that knot as much as he would need.

300
00:20:16,883 --> 00:20:21,787
Ayeshaرضى الله عنه was going to Hajj(حَجْ); And she heard some men talking outside.

301
00:20:22,141 --> 00:20:26,183
And one of them is asking; he's giving them a quiz.

302
00:20:27,223 --> 00:20:27,630
He said;

303
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:29,025
من امن الناس على أخى؟

304
00:20:29,439 --> 00:20:31,707
Who did the greatest favor on his brother?

305
00:20:31,887 --> 00:20:35,964
He's asking these men, who did the biggest favor to his brother?

306
00:20:36,398 --> 00:20:41,294
Ayesha(عائشه) from inside her Hawdij(هودج) from over the camel; She responded and said;

307
00:20:41,324 --> 00:20:45,718
Musa(موسى); he is the one who did the biggest favour on his brother Haroon(هارون).

308
00:20:45,878 --> 00:20:50,418
Because the biggest favour is that Musa(موسى) asked Allah to make Haroon(هارون) a prophet.

309
00:20:51,058 --> 00:20:53,115
What bigger favour could you do for your brother?

310
00:20:53,875 --> 00:20:55,835
He asked Allah; Oh Allah! make my brother a prophet.

311
00:20:56,395 --> 00:21:00,195
No brother has done his brother a favour like Musa(موسى) has done; Haroon(هارون).

312
00:21:00,628 --> 00:21:05,005
وَاجْعَل لِّي وَزِيرًا مِّنْ أَهْلِي۝

313
00:21:05,438 --> 00:21:08,145
And appoint for me a helper from my family.

314
00:21:08,458 --> 00:21:10,479
هَارُونَ أَخِى۝

315
00:21:10,879 --> 00:21:12,326
Haroon(هارون); My brother.

316
00:21:12,566 --> 00:21:19,377
And then notice here the rules of brotherhood in Islam are in the following Ayaat(آيات).

317
00:21:20,050 --> 00:21:22,824
Why does he want help from his brother Haroon(هارون)?

318
00:21:23,044 --> 00:21:26,187
اشْدُدْ بِهِ أَزْرِي۝

319
00:21:26,404 --> 00:21:28,187
To increase my strength with him.

320
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:31,287
Your brother and you are stronger together.

321
00:21:31,947 --> 00:21:34,187
That's one purpose of brotherhood in Islam.

322
00:21:34,407 --> 00:21:36,254
You become stronger when you have a brother.

323
00:21:36,520 --> 00:21:39,400
When you're alone, you're not as strong as when you have a brother.

324
00:21:39,660 --> 00:21:42,807
And that's why Rasool Allah ﷺ has always told us to be with the Jama'ah(جماعة).

325
00:21:43,034 --> 00:21:46,480
Don't think that you can survive alone in the wilderness outside.

326
00:21:46,539 --> 00:21:53,813
Outside; is a jungle; It's a jungle and you need to be with the Muslims because you are like sheep.

327
00:21:53,893 --> 00:21:55,119
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

328
00:21:55,339 --> 00:21:57,373
إنما يأكل الذئب الغنم القاصية

329
00:21:57,485 --> 00:22:00,393
The wolf eats from the stray sheep.

330
00:22:01,313 --> 00:22:04,115
The wolf will not attack the pack; the flock.

331
00:22:04,254 --> 00:22:06,520
The wolf will attack the sheep which is alone.

332
00:22:07,114 --> 00:22:08,294
اشْدُدْ بِهِ أَزْرِي۝

333
00:22:08,364 --> 00:22:09,147
That's number one.

334
00:22:09,294 --> 00:22:12,831
And then; and let him share my task.

335
00:22:13,265 --> 00:22:15,905
So he will help me in my tasks.

336
00:22:16,271 --> 00:22:20,030
Brotherhood in Islam is not for worldly benefit or gain.

337
00:22:20,770 --> 00:22:22,764
Brotherhood in Islam is for;

338
00:22:23,724 --> 00:22:26,504
كَىْ نُسَبِّحَكَ كَثِيرًا۝

339
00:22:26,877 --> 00:22:29,331
وَنَذْكُرَكَ كَثِيرًا۝

340
00:22:29,718 --> 00:22:33,978
إِنَّكَ كُنتَ بِنَا بَصِيرًا۝

341
00:22:34,206 --> 00:22:41,245
That we may glorify You much, and remember You much, verily You are of us ever a well-seer.

342
00:22:41,978 --> 00:22:45,092
We can worship You together; That's why I want to have a brother.

343
00:22:45,219 --> 00:22:48,779
So that, we can both worship Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and make Tasbeeh(تسبيه) and Dhikr(ذكر) for Allah.

344
00:22:49,572 --> 00:22:50,737
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said;

345
00:22:50,890 --> 00:22:55,590
قَالَ قَدْ أُوتِيتَ سُؤْلَكَ يَا مُوسَىٰ۝

346
00:22:55,857 --> 00:22:59,702
Allah said; You are granted your request, Oh Musa(موسى)!.

347
00:23:00,008 --> 00:23:01,502
Allah granted him his request.

348
00:23:01,908 --> 00:23:08,948
Now, there are few other points which Musa(موسى) wants to ask Allahسُبحانه وتعالى about.

349
00:23:09,554 --> 00:23:13,628
Musa(موسى) has left Egypt because of the murder case that happened.

350
00:23:14,621 --> 00:23:17,592
There was a warrant against Musa(موسى).

351
00:23:18,565 --> 00:23:21,058
So, he wants to ask about Allahسُبحانه وتعالى about this.

352
00:23:21,118 --> 00:23:21,392
He says;

353
00:23:21,452 --> 00:23:25,262
قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّى قَتَلْتُ مِنْهُمْ نَفْسًا فَأَخَافُ أَن يَقْتُلُونِ۝

354
00:23:25,903 --> 00:23:30,482
He said; My Lord! I have killed a man among them and I fear that they may kill me.

355
00:23:30,809 --> 00:23:38,606
قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّى قَتَلْتُ مِنْهُمْ نَفْسًا فَأَخَافُ أَن يَقْتُلُونِ۝

356
00:23:39,339 --> 00:23:48,143
وَأَخِى هَٰرُونُ هُوَ أَفْصَحُ مِنِّى لِسَانًا فَأَرْسِلْهُ مَعِىَ رِدْءًا يُصَدِّقُنِىٓ ۖ

357
00:23:48,383 --> 00:23:52,769
إِنِّىٓ أَخَافُ أَن يُكَذِّبُونِ۝

358
00:23:53,203 --> 00:24:02,263
قَالَ سَنَشُدُّ عَضُدَكَ بِأَخِيكَ وَنَجْعَلُ لَكُمَا سُلْطَٰنًا فَلَا يَصِلُونَ إِلَيْكُمَا ۚ

359
00:24:02,570 --> 00:24:09,118
بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآ أَنتُمَا وَمَنِ ٱتَّبَعَكُمَا ٱلْغَٰلِبُونَ۝

360
00:24:09,337 --> 00:24:15,728
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; he said, my Lord! I have killed a man among them and I fear that they will kill me.

361
00:24:16,222 --> 00:24:21,115
And my brother; Haroon(هارون), he is more eloquent in speech than me; He's better in speaking.

362
00:24:21,455 --> 00:24:24,247
So, send him with me as a helper to confirm me.

363
00:24:24,487 --> 00:24:26,987
Verily, I fear that they will belie me.

364
00:24:27,407 --> 00:24:33,216
Allah said; We will strengthen your arm through your brother and give you both power.

365
00:24:33,363 --> 00:24:37,743
So, they shall not be able to harm you with our Ayaat(آيات).

366
00:24:37,943 --> 00:24:42,053
You two as well as those who follow you will be victorious.

367
00:24:44,126 --> 00:24:48,460
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى); now to go to Firaun(فرعون).

368
00:24:49,113 --> 00:24:53,961
Go with your brother to Firaun(فرعون) and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gave him advice.

369
00:24:54,247 --> 00:25:00,241
اذْهَبَا إِلَى فِرْعَوْنَ إِنَّهُ طَغَى۝

370
00:25:00,701 --> 00:25:08,303
فَقُولَا لَهُ قَوْلًا لَيِّنًا لَعَلَّهُ يَتَذَكَّرُ أَوْ يَخْشَى۝

371
00:25:08,856 --> 00:25:14,796
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; Go both of you to Pharaoh, verily he has transgressed.

372
00:25:15,296 --> 00:25:16,404
And what is the advice?

373
00:25:16,442 --> 00:25:20,809
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; and speak to him mildly.

374
00:25:21,549 --> 00:25:23,016
قَوْلًا لَيِّنًا

375
00:25:23,196 --> 00:25:25,976
Layyin(لَيِّن) means, soft and mild.

376
00:25:27,549 --> 00:25:29,041
What is the wisdom behind that?

377
00:25:29,107 --> 00:25:30,337
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

378
00:25:30,397 --> 00:25:32,482
لَعَلَّهُ يَتَذَكَّرُ أَوْ يَخْشَى۝

379
00:25:32,767 --> 00:25:36,135
Perhaps, he may accept admonition or fear Allah.

380
00:25:37,210 --> 00:25:42,497
If you speak to someone mildly and softly, there is a possibility that, he will fear Allah and he would remember.

381
00:25:42,803 --> 00:25:45,856
If you speak to them roughly, most likely they won't.

382
00:25:47,843 --> 00:25:51,724
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is telling Musa(موسى) the manners of Da'wah(دعوة).

383
00:25:52,003 --> 00:25:58,641
It has to be done in a soft manner; It has to be done in a mild way; That is how it should be done.

384
00:26:01,021 --> 00:26:05,747
I want to mention one thing in regards to Da'wah(دعوة) here.

385
00:26:05,777 --> 00:26:16,594
Sometimes we think that part of being mild in Da'wah(دعوة) is to not threaten the other side or make them worry.

386
00:26:17,681 --> 00:26:28,948
Sometimes in our Da'wah(دعوة); we tell the people about Islam but we shy away from mentioning to them the consequences of not believing.

387
00:26:29,942 --> 00:26:34,935
We sometimes hold back telling the people, if you don't believe, this is what will happen to you; You will be in hellfire.

388
00:26:36,028 --> 00:26:37,695
We think that, that is too harsh.

389
00:26:38,149 --> 00:26:39,455
Is that true or not?

390
00:26:40,262 --> 00:26:42,675
We find here the answer in the Ayaat(آيات).

391
00:26:44,221 --> 00:26:52,696
The Ayah(آية) that says talk to Firaun(فرعون) in a mild fashion is Ayah(آية) forty four in Surah-Taha(سورة طه).

392
00:26:52,980 --> 00:27:03,610
Ayah(آية) forty eight in Surah-Taha(سورة طه); Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is telling that Musa(موسى) is saying to Firaun(فرعون);

393
00:27:04,196 --> 00:27:08,690
إِنَّا قَدْ أُوحِىَ إِلَيْنَآ أَنَّ ٱلْعَذَابَ عَلَىٰ مَن كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلَّىٰ۝

394
00:27:09,530 --> 00:27:18,270
Musa(موسى) is telling Firaun(فرعون); Truly it has been revealed to us that torment will be for him, who denies and turns away from Allah.

395
00:27:19,230 --> 00:27:25,423
 So Musa(موسى) is telling Firaun(فرعون); I have received revelation that if you don't believe in Allah, you will be punished in hellfire.

396
00:27:26,377 --> 00:27:31,680
Therefore, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى tells us that we should be mild and soft in our Da'wah(دعوة).

397
00:27:31,740 --> 00:27:33,574
But this is not part of it.

398
00:27:33,634 --> 00:27:34,548
Why?

399
00:27:34,728 --> 00:27:37,136
Because this is part of the honesty of conveying the message.

400
00:27:37,503 --> 00:27:41,083
The Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah have been given an Amanah(امانة); trust.

401
00:27:41,776 --> 00:27:43,269
And they have to be honest.

402
00:27:43,829 --> 00:27:46,722
They cannot hold back information from people.

403
00:27:47,022 --> 00:27:48,549
They have to tell them the truth.

404
00:27:48,809 --> 00:27:50,266
بَشِيرًا وَنَذِيرًا

405
00:27:50,515 --> 00:27:53,490
To give them the glad tidings and to give them the warning.

406
00:27:53,743 --> 00:27:58,176
If you believe; you would receive Jannah(جنة); If you don't believe; you would receive Hellfire.

407
00:27:58,716 --> 00:28:01,500
Anyway, Musa(موسى) and Haroon(هارون), they said;

408
00:28:01,573 --> 00:28:04,716
قَالَا رَبَّنَاۤ إِنَّنَا نَخَافُ أَن یَفۡرُطَ عَلَیۡنَاۤ أَوۡ أَن یَطۡغَىٰ۝

409
00:28:04,740 --> 00:28:10,557
Oh Allah! We fear that they should hasten to punish us or lest, they should transgress.

410
00:28:10,587 --> 00:28:16,761
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told them; fear not, verily, I am with you both hearing and seeing.

411
00:28:17,995 --> 00:28:22,704
So Musa(موسى) and Haroon(هارون); they had different conversations with Firaun(فرعون)

412
00:28:22,978 --> 00:28:26,284
and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى mentions that in many parts of Qur'an.

413
00:28:26,471 --> 00:28:28,058
We'll talk about this one here.

414
00:28:28,691 --> 00:28:32,752
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in many Ayaat(آيات) mentions this.

415
00:28:32,812 --> 00:28:35,546
This one is in Surat(سورت) Ash-Shu'ara(الشعراء).

416
00:28:36,039 --> 00:28:42,007
When Musa(موسى) went to Firaun(فرعون) and asked him to believe in Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

417
00:28:43,147 --> 00:28:50,545
Firaun(فرعون) immediately started reminding Musa(موسى) with his previous crime.

418
00:28:52,145 --> 00:28:56,985
And he also started reminding Musa(موسى) with his favours on him.

419
00:28:59,192 --> 00:29:00,658
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

420
00:29:00,865 --> 00:29:10,851
قَالَ أَلَمْ نُرَبِّكَ فِينَا وَلِيدًا وَلَبِثْتَ فِينَا مِنْ عُمُرِكَ سِنِينَ۝

421
00:29:11,145 --> 00:29:16,499
Pharaoh said to Musa(موسى); Did we not bring you up among us as a child?

422
00:29:16,725 --> 00:29:21,388
And we did dwell many years and you did dwell many years of your life with us.

423
00:29:21,795 --> 00:29:25,361
I'm the one who raised you up; I'm the one who fed you; I'm the one who took care of you.

424
00:29:25,721 --> 00:29:27,708
And this is what you end up doing to me.

425
00:29:28,121 --> 00:29:29,261
And the other thing he said;

426
00:29:29,408 --> 00:29:38,478
وَفَعَلْتَ فَعْلَتَكَ ٱلَّتِى فَعَلْتَ وَأَنتَ مِنَ ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ۝

427
00:29:38,618 --> 00:29:41,192
And you did your deed, which you did.

428
00:29:41,279 --> 00:29:42,385
He's talking about what?

429
00:29:42,812 --> 00:29:43,765
The crime of killing.

430
00:29:44,038 --> 00:29:47,805
And you were one of the ungrates; you were ungrateful.

431
00:29:48,205 --> 00:29:51,478
We took care of you and then you ended up, killing one of our people.

432
00:29:52,071 --> 00:29:55,525
The response of Musa(موسى) was amazing.

433
00:29:55,585 --> 00:29:57,235
Very interesting response.

434
00:29:57,682 --> 00:30:01,862
Firaun(فرعون) has done Musa(موسى) a favour right; A big favour.

435
00:30:02,442 --> 00:30:11,706
He raised him up for years in his palace as an adopted son and took care of him for all of his life.

436
00:30:12,346 --> 00:30:15,906
How could you now come and talk to me this way?

437
00:30:16,326 --> 00:30:17,373
It's a big favor.

438
00:30:17,713 --> 00:30:20,240
But look at the response of Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى).

439
00:30:20,840 --> 00:30:21,733
He said;

440
00:30:21,900 --> 00:30:36,041
وَتِلْكَ نِعْمَةٌ تَمُنُّهَا عَلَىَّ أَنْ عَبَّدتَّ بَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ۝

441
00:30:36,253 --> 00:30:42,763
Is this a favor you are telling me about, when you have enslave the children of Israel(اسرائيل)?

442
00:30:43,169 --> 00:30:47,994
What was the reason, Musa(موسى) was raised up in the house of Firaun(فرعون)?

443
00:30:49,801 --> 00:30:52,948
It is because of the oppression of Firaun(فرعون) to Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

444
00:30:53,974 --> 00:30:59,402
If it wasn't for that oppression, Musa(موسى) would have been raised by his own parents; He did not need Firaun(فرعون).

445
00:31:00,735 --> 00:31:02,315
He did not need Firaun(فرعون).

446
00:31:02,694 --> 00:31:10,180
The only reason; why Musa(موسى) was raised by Firaun(فرعون) is because of the oppression of Firaun(فرعون) against Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

447
00:31:10,974 --> 00:31:14,961
And because of that oppression, he ended up raising up Musa(موسى).

448
00:31:14,991 --> 00:31:18,603
Otherwise Musa(موسى) would have been in his house, his mother would not put him in the river.

449
00:31:19,016 --> 00:31:21,773
His mother put him in a river because of the fear of Firaun(فرعون).

450
00:31:22,093 --> 00:31:26,702
If Firaun(فرعون) was not oppressive and Zalim(ظالم); he would have been raised in his own house.

451
00:31:27,262 --> 00:31:30,468
So, Musa(موسى) is telling him; what favor are you talking about? That's not the favor.

452
00:31:30,709 --> 00:31:33,381
That is because of your oppression against Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

453
00:31:33,854 --> 00:31:35,574
So don't tell me that, that's a favor.

454
00:31:36,054 --> 00:31:37,521
And then he talked about the crime.

455
00:31:37,794 --> 00:31:41,091
He Musa عليه السلام said;

456
00:31:41,257 --> 00:31:43,217
قَالَ فَعَلْتُهَا إِذًا وَأَنَا مِنَ الضَّالِّينَ۝

457
00:31:43,337 --> 00:31:46,677
I did it in a time of ignorance; I was ignorant at the time.

458
00:31:47,004 --> 00:32:01,091
فَفَرَرْتُ مِنكُمْ لَمَّا خِفْتُكُمْ فَوَهَبَ لِى رَبِّى حُكْمًا وَجَعَلَنِى مِنَ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ۝

459
00:32:01,271 --> 00:32:06,153
And then I ran away from you and then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given me the message.

460
00:32:06,927 --> 00:32:09,520
So don't hold me accountable for something that I did then.

461
00:32:09,733 --> 00:32:11,371
Because at that time I was ignorant.

462
00:32:11,691 --> 00:32:15,058
But now, I have the message from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

463
00:32:15,824 --> 00:32:17,230
وَجَعَلَنِى مِنَ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ۝

464
00:32:17,356 --> 00:32:18,643
He made me of the messengers.

465
00:32:18,803 --> 00:32:24,530
قَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ وَمَا رَبُّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ۝

466
00:32:24,763 --> 00:32:26,829
قَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ وَمَا رَبُّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ۝

467
00:32:27,303 --> 00:32:29,982
Firaun(فرعون) said; who is; who is the God of the world; Who is He?

468
00:32:30,529 --> 00:32:32,702
Who are you talking about; Who's your Lord?

469
00:32:33,476 --> 00:32:34,402
Musa(موسى) said;

470
00:32:34,769 --> 00:32:49,433
قَالَ رَبُّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَآ ۖ إِن كُنتُم مُّوقِنِينَ۝

471
00:32:49,898 --> 00:32:54,224
He said; The Lord of the Heavens and the Earth and all that is in between them.

472
00:32:54,470 --> 00:32:56,730
If you seek to be convinced with certainty.

473
00:32:57,577 --> 00:32:59,354
Musa(موسى) is talking serious.

474
00:32:59,801 --> 00:33:03,574
He's saying; Allah is the Lord of the Heavens and the Earth.

475
00:33:03,967 --> 00:33:08,696
Firaun(فرعون) wants to turn it into joke and entertainment.

476
00:33:08,936 --> 00:33:11,323
So, he started making fun of Musa(موسى).

477
00:33:11,563 --> 00:33:19,438
قَالَ لِمَنْ حَوْلَهُۥٓ أَلَا تَسْتَمِعُونَ۝

478
00:33:20,172 --> 00:33:27,076
So, he started to make fool out of Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى); mocking at Syedina Musaعليه السلام .

479
00:33:27,236 --> 00:33:30,303
Musa(موسى) did not respond to that; he was not sidetracked.

480
00:33:30,889 --> 00:33:32,131
Musa(موسى) continued and said;

481
00:33:32,211 --> 00:33:35,071
قَالَ رَبُّكُمْ وَرَبُّ آبَائِكُمُ الْأَوَّلِينَ۝

482
00:33:35,318 --> 00:33:38,638
He is your Lord and the Lord of your forefathers before you.

483
00:33:40,082 --> 00:33:42,295
Now, Firaun(فرعون) got angry.

484
00:33:42,835 --> 00:33:54,033
قَالَ إِنَّ رَسُولَكُمُ ٱلَّذِىٓ أُرْسِلَ إِلَيْكُمْ لَمَجْنُونٌ۝

485
00:33:54,153 --> 00:33:57,438
He said; the messenger who is sent to you is crazy.

486
00:33:58,131 --> 00:34:03,405
Now, he started getting serious and angry and he is accusing Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) of insanity.

487
00:34:04,005 --> 00:34:06,639
Musa(موسى) did not respond to that either and he continued.

488
00:34:06,985 --> 00:34:07,965
Look at the Daiyah(داعيه);

489
00:34:08,392 --> 00:34:21,891
قَالَ رَبُّ ٱلْمَشْرِقِ وَٱلْمَغْرِبِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَآ ۖ إِن كُنتُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ۝

490
00:34:22,123 --> 00:34:27,784
He is the Lord of the East and the West and everything in between, if you have any understanding.

491
00:34:27,931 --> 00:34:31,683
And this is an important lesson of Da'wah(دعوة); Don't protect your own self in Da'wah(دعوة).

492
00:34:31,743 --> 00:34:35,509
We would be talking with somebody about Da'wah(دعوة); giving them the message;

493
00:34:35,715 --> 00:34:38,777
they will attack us; we start defending our ownselves.

494
00:34:39,111 --> 00:34:42,524
And we'll get into the conversation and the debate of defending our ownselves.

495
00:34:42,651 --> 00:34:46,300
Firaun(فرعون) starts accusing him; Musa(موسى) is continuing with the signs of Allah.

496
00:34:47,287 --> 00:34:55,102
And now, Firaon(فرعون) goes from the next step; He started with mockery and then accusing and then now, threatening.

497
00:34:55,328 --> 00:35:05,338
قَالَ لَئِنِ ٱتَّخَذْتَ إِلَٰهًا غَيْرِى لَأَجْعَلَنَّكَ مِنَ ٱلْمَسْجُونِينَ۝

498
00:35:05,405 --> 00:35:09,340
If you take any other God beside me, I will throw you in jail.

499
00:35:11,433 --> 00:35:12,026
Musa(موسى) said;

500
00:35:12,106 --> 00:35:13,698
قَالَ أَوَلَوْ جِئْتُكَ بِشَىْءٍۢ مُّبِينٍۢ۝

501
00:35:13,728 --> 00:35:15,925
What, if I bring you with clear signs from Allah.

502
00:35:16,478 --> 00:35:18,518
Firaun(فرعون) told him; show me what you have.

503
00:35:19,025 --> 00:35:20,147
Musa(موسى) threw his stick.

504
00:35:20,233 --> 00:35:21,687
فَإِذَا هِىَ ثُعْبَانٌ مُّبِينٌ۝

505
00:35:21,747 --> 00:35:22,737
It turned into a snake.

506
00:35:22,960 --> 00:35:25,212
وَنَزَعَ يَدَهُۥ فَإِذَا هِىَ بَيْضَآءُ لِلنَّٰظِرِينَ۝

507
00:35:25,248 --> 00:35:32,065
And he took out his hand from under his arm and it was white for all of them around him.

508
00:35:32,418 --> 00:35:37,914
Now, Firaun(فرعون) said that Musa(موسى) is a magician.

509
00:35:38,488 --> 00:35:42,814
قَالَ لِلْمَلَإِ حَوْلَهُۥٓ إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَسَٰحِرٌ عَلِيمٌ۝

510
00:35:43,585 --> 00:35:50,600
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) the Ayaat(آيات).

511
00:35:52,089 --> 00:36:02,417
Firaun(فرعون) refuse to follow the signs, which he has seen with his own eyes and accused Musa of being a sorcerer; a magician.

512
00:36:04,012 --> 00:36:15,323
Firaun(فرعون) announced that, he will gather all of the magicians of Egypt and bring them to challenge Syedina Musaعليه السلام.

513
00:36:16,270 --> 00:36:17,730
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

514
00:36:18,003 --> 00:36:24,877
وَلَقَدْ أَرَيْنَٰهُ ءَايَٰتِنَا كُلَّهَا فَكَذَّبَ وَأَبَىٰ۝

515
00:36:25,370 --> 00:36:29,557
We showed Firaun(فرعون) all of our signs; Nevertheless, he still rejected and refused.

516
00:36:29,963 --> 00:36:37,137
قَالَ أَجِئْتَنَا لِتُخْرِجَنَا مِنْ أَرْضِنَا بِسِحْرِكَ يَٰمُوسَىٰ۝

517
00:36:37,629 --> 00:36:41,216
Oh Musa(موسى)! do you want to drive us out of our land with your magic.

518
00:36:41,983 --> 00:36:48,760
So, he accused Musa(موسى) of trying to take over the government and drive them out of the land.

519
00:36:49,826 --> 00:36:52,280
This is the thing he accused Musa(موسى) of doing.

520
00:36:52,760 --> 00:36:54,079
لِتُخْرِجَنَا مِنْ أَرْضِنَا

521
00:36:54,109 --> 00:36:58,046
You want to drive us out of our land, take over the government and kick us out.

522
00:36:58,999 --> 00:37:01,129
He said; you want to do that with your magic.

523
00:37:01,702 --> 00:37:03,442
We have stronger magic than yours.

524
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:19,077
فَلَنَأْتِيَنَّكَ بِسِحْرٍۢ مِّثْلِهِۦ فَٱجْعَلْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَّا نُخْلِفُهُۥ نَحْنُ وَلَآ أَنتَ مَكَانًا سُوًى۝

525
00:37:19,520 --> 00:37:23,044
We going to bring you with magic similar to it and better.

526
00:37:24,196 --> 00:37:28,254
فَٱجْعَلْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَّا نُخْلِفُهُۥ نَحْنُ وَلَآ أَنتَ مَكَانًا سُوًى۝

527
00:37:28,575 --> 00:37:30,468
So, let's have an appointed time.

528
00:37:31,348 --> 00:37:35,081
Musa(موسى) chose the day of Al-Zeenah(الزينه).

529
00:37:35,568 --> 00:37:37,998
This is the Festival of the people of Egypt.

530
00:37:38,632 --> 00:37:43,252
On that day, all of the people would gather together and they would have a big celebration.

531
00:37:43,505 --> 00:37:48,604
Musa(موسى) chose that day because he wants everybody to be there and he wants everyone to see the signs of Allah.

532
00:37:49,051 --> 00:37:56,614
قَالَ مَوْعِدُكُمْ يَوْمُ ٱلزِّينَةِ وَأَن يُحْشَرَ ٱلنَّاسُ ضُحًى۝

533
00:37:56,921 --> 00:38:01,087
The appointed time is your festival day and we'll meet in the early morning.

534
00:38:01,201 --> 00:38:04,524
When all of the people come together, then we're gonna start our competition.

535
00:38:04,831 --> 00:38:10,544
فَتَوَلَّىٰ فِرْعَوْنُ فَجَمَعَ كَيْدَهُۥ ثُمَّ أَتَىٰ۝

536
00:38:11,002 --> 00:38:15,237
Firaun(فرعون) left and he brought together all of his strength and power.

537
00:38:15,771 --> 00:38:26,708
قَالَ لَهُم مُّوسَىٰ وَيْلَكُمْ لَا تَفْتَرُواْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ كَذِبًا فَيُسْحِتَكُم بِعَذَابٍۢ ۖ

538
00:38:26,968 --> 00:38:32,629
Musa(موسى); when he saw all of the magicians present,

539
00:38:33,235 --> 00:38:41,983
it says in another Ayah(آية) that Firaun(فرعون) has sent to all of the towns of Egypt to gather all of the magicians.

540
00:38:42,557 --> 00:38:46,024
He has sent his orders to bring all of the magicians from Egypt.

541
00:38:46,304 --> 00:38:48,137
What was the role of the magicians in Egypt?

542
00:38:48,591 --> 00:38:53,224
First of all, we need to realize that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, when He sends a prophet;

543
00:38:54,097 --> 00:39:00,827
He provides the Nabi(نَبِي) with miracles that challenge the people in their field of expertise.

544
00:39:01,600 --> 00:39:11,725
So the people of Egypt; the most high ranking science that they had; and their field of expertise was; the field of magic.

545
00:39:12,825 --> 00:39:21,154
They were very powerful in that field and maybe the world, until today has never seen such powerful magic like; what existed in Egypt.

546
00:39:21,494 --> 00:39:23,295
They were the top in magic.

547
00:39:23,595 --> 00:39:31,100
Firaun(فرعون) used to use the magicians to control and dominate the minds of the society.

548
00:39:32,113 --> 00:39:35,333
He would use them to influence and control the minds of people.

549
00:39:35,713 --> 00:39:37,485
So these were working with Firaun(فرعون).

550
00:39:37,691 --> 00:39:39,364
And that's why they say in another Ayah(آية).

551
00:39:39,394 --> 00:39:40,824
وَمَآ أَكْرَهْتَنَا عَلَيْهِ مِنَ ٱلسِّحْرِ ۗ

552
00:39:41,024 --> 00:39:42,437
They were forced to learn this.

553
00:39:42,510 --> 00:39:46,184
And Firaun(فرعون) would have schools, where they would teach them the magic.

554
00:39:46,403 --> 00:39:50,409
And then he would use it to control the minds of people; through magic.

555
00:39:50,796 --> 00:39:54,329
And to give the people the impression, that Firaun(فرعون) is God.

556
00:39:54,463 --> 00:39:58,523
And these magicians would commit these strange acts of magic

557
00:39:58,935 --> 00:40:04,316
and they will do it in the name of Firaun(فرعون) and that is how, they control the lives of people in Egypt.

558
00:40:05,059 --> 00:40:12,260
But Firaun(فرعون) was very terrified from this single man Syedina Musaعليه السلام.

559
00:40:12,454 --> 00:40:14,854
So, he didn't bring one magician or two.

560
00:40:14,954 --> 00:40:17,894
He brought the best magicians that Egypt could offer.

561
00:40:19,087 --> 00:40:22,430
And there are different narrations; We don't know how much for sure.

562
00:40:22,910 --> 00:40:26,155
Ibn-e-Ashaab(ابن اسحاب) goes as far as saying; 15,000

563
00:40:26,915 --> 00:40:28,735
but Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) says; 70.

564
00:40:29,421 --> 00:40:34,568
So let's go with the least and that is the narration of Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) seventy magicians.

565
00:40:35,395 --> 00:40:38,002
These 70 magicians were standing in front of Musa(موسى).

566
00:40:38,662 --> 00:40:44,601
Musa(موسى); his point is not to win; His point is to give Da'wah(دعوة).

567
00:40:45,674 --> 00:40:47,594
So he wanted to give them another chance.

568
00:40:48,448 --> 00:40:49,528
So Musa(موسى) told them;

569
00:40:49,628 --> 00:41:00,363
قَالَ لَهُم مُّوسَىٰ وَيْلَكُمْ لَا تَفْتَرُواْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ كَذِبًا فَيُسْحِتَكُم بِعَذَابٍۢ ۖ

570
00:41:00,877 --> 00:41:03,723
وَقَدْ خَابَ مَنِ ٱفْتَرَىٰ۝

571
00:41:04,107 --> 00:41:11,406
Moses said to them; Woe unto you invent not a lie against Allah, lest He should destroy you completely by a torment.

572
00:41:11,664 --> 00:41:15,117
And surely he who invents a lie against Allah will fail miserably.

573
00:41:15,537 --> 00:41:16,798
He's giving them another chance.

574
00:41:16,828 --> 00:41:19,570
He's saying; this is a lie against the Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

575
00:41:19,983 --> 00:41:22,988
And if you continue with that; you will end up failing.

576
00:41:23,702 --> 00:41:27,962
These words were discussed by the magicians.

577
00:41:28,169 --> 00:41:29,509
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

578
00:41:29,762 --> 00:41:37,250
فَتَنَٰزَعُوٓاْ أَمْرَهُم بَيْنَهُمْ وَأَسَرُّواْ ٱلنَّجْوَىٰ۝

579
00:41:37,693 --> 00:41:43,097
Allah says; then they debated with one another; what they must do and they kept their talk secret.

580
00:41:44,477 --> 00:41:47,314
They were discussing; is this man really a prophet or is he a magician?

581
00:41:48,612 --> 00:41:51,572
In the end, they settled the argument and said he's a magician.

582
00:41:52,125 --> 00:41:54,898
And this is our plan and this is what we're going to do.

583
00:41:56,444 --> 00:41:59,578
And Firaun(فرعون) said and they said with him;

584
00:41:59,804 --> 00:42:15,850
قَالُوٓاْ إِنْ هَٰذَٰنِ لَسَٰحِرَٰنِ يُرِيدَانِ أَن يُخْرِجَاكُم مِّنْ أَرْضِكُم بِسِحْرِهِمَا وَيَذْهَبَا بِطَرِيقَتِكُمُ ٱلْمُثْلَىٰ۝

585
00:42:16,477 --> 00:42:22,618
These are two magicians; Their object is to drive you out of your land with their magic and overcome your chiefs and nobles.

586
00:42:22,845 --> 00:42:27,950
فَأَجْمِعُواْ كَيْدَكُمْ ثُمَّ ٱئْتُواْ صَفًّا ۚ

587
00:42:28,117 --> 00:42:32,190
وَقَدْ أَفْلَحَ ٱلْيَوْمَ مَنِ ٱسْتَعْلَىٰ۝

588
00:42:32,710 --> 00:42:39,323
So, devise your plot and then assemble in a line and whoever overcomes this day, will be indeed successful.

589
00:42:39,736 --> 00:42:41,595
He told them; assemble in a line.

590
00:42:42,029 --> 00:42:43,989
So imagine with me; this is a festival.

591
00:42:44,555 --> 00:42:48,654
All of the people of Egypt are there; surrounding this battlefield.

592
00:42:50,107 --> 00:42:56,181
And one side of the battlefield; 70 magicians lined up with all of their equipment.

593
00:42:57,142 --> 00:43:01,959
And on the other side; Musa(موسى) standing alone and his brother behind him.

594
00:43:03,213 --> 00:43:07,518
Imagine the scene; 70 magicians; that is the minimum number,

595
00:43:07,685 --> 00:43:14,393
imagine it's 15,000, in ranks; lines with all of their equipment; with all of their tools.

596
00:43:14,973 --> 00:43:20,513
And Musa(موسى) is standing alone on the other side; And all of the people of Egypt are surrounding them and watching.

597
00:43:22,290 --> 00:43:24,038
And they devise their plan.

598
00:43:25,125 --> 00:43:25,985
So, they said;

599
00:43:26,298 --> 00:43:39,353
قَالُواْ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِمَّآ أَن تُلْقِىَ وَإِمَّآ أَن نَّكُونَ أَوَّلَ مَنْ أَلْقَىٰ۝

600
00:43:39,747 --> 00:43:46,593
Oh Musa(موسى)! Either you throw your stick first or we will be the first to throw.

601
00:43:47,427 --> 00:43:48,538
قَالَ بَلْ أَلْقُواْ ۖ

602
00:43:48,711 --> 00:43:51,045
He said; throw your sticks.

603
00:43:51,925 --> 00:43:54,698
So they threw their sticks and their ropes.

604
00:43:55,011 --> 00:43:56,406
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

605
00:43:56,591 --> 00:44:06,193
فَإِذَا حِبَالُهُمْ وَعِصِيُّهُمْ يُخَيَّلُ إِلَيْهِ مِن سِحْرِهِمْ أَنَّهَا تَسْعَىٰ۝

606
00:44:06,713 --> 00:44:14,384
Then behold their ropes and their sticks by their magic, appeared to him as though they moved fast.

607
00:44:15,491 --> 00:44:22,682
And these were not amateur magicians or weak in their field.

608
00:44:22,954 --> 00:44:28,422
These were strong professional and they were the best, maybe the world has ever seen in magic.

609
00:44:28,695 --> 00:44:30,951
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says in the other Ayah(آية);

610
00:44:31,105 --> 00:44:36,305
قَالَ أَلْقُواْ ۖ فَلَمَّآ أَلْقَوْاْ سَحَرُوٓاْ أَعْيُنَ ٱلنَّاسِ وَٱسْتَرْهَبُوهُمْ وَجَآءُو بِسِحْرٍ عَظِيمٍۢ۝

611
00:44:36,634 --> 00:44:46,481
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; When they threw their sticks and their ropes; they have made magic and illusion on the eyes of people.

612
00:44:46,841 --> 00:44:48,115
وَٱسْتَرْهَبُوهُمْ

613
00:44:48,775 --> 00:44:51,008
They put fear in the hearts of people.

614
00:44:51,128 --> 00:44:52,481
وَجَآءُو بِسِحْرٍ عَظِيمٍۢ۝

615
00:44:52,511 --> 00:44:55,024
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is saying; This is great magic.

616
00:44:55,666 --> 00:44:57,793
Imagine; how powerful it would have been.

617
00:44:58,543 --> 00:44:59,103
First of all;

618
00:44:59,133 --> 00:45:00,335
سَحَرُوٓاْ أَعْيُنَ ٱلنَّاسِ

619
00:45:01,159 --> 00:45:02,097
أَعْيُنَ ٱلنَّاسِ

620
00:45:02,219 --> 00:45:09,656
The magic was on the eyes of men; meaning that, These sticks and ropes weren't really snakes.

621
00:45:10,162 --> 00:45:13,217
Because we cannot give life to the dead.

622
00:45:13,970 --> 00:45:16,830
Therefore, it was an illusion; an optical illusion.

623
00:45:17,224 --> 00:45:18,344
That is, what it is.

624
00:45:18,597 --> 00:45:23,348
Because, we do not control the difference between life and death and that is; Ar-Rooh(الروح).

625
00:45:24,075 --> 00:45:25,747
ٱلرُّوحُ مِنْ أَمْرِ رَبِّى

626
00:45:26,221 --> 00:45:27,235
يَسْـَٔلُونَكَ عَنِ ٱلرُّوحِ ۖ

627
00:45:27,355 --> 00:45:28,948
They ask you about the soul.

628
00:45:29,335 --> 00:45:31,022
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is telling Muhammadﷺ;

629
00:45:31,052 --> 00:45:34,062
قُلِ ٱلرُّوحُ مِنْ أَمْرِ رَبِّى وَمَآ أُوتِيتُم مِّنَ ٱلْعِلْمِ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا۝

630
00:45:34,237 --> 00:45:39,069
Tell them that, the soul; the knowledge of the soul belongs to Allah and you only have little knowledge.

631
00:45:39,462 --> 00:45:41,789
This is something that only Allahسُبحانه وتعالى controls.

632
00:45:41,869 --> 00:45:43,862
So this magic was an illusion.

633
00:45:44,222 --> 00:45:45,487
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

634
00:45:45,517 --> 00:45:46,567
وَٱسْتَرْهَبُوهُمْ

635
00:45:46,793 --> 00:45:51,536
When  the people saw this, they were afraid and terrified.

636
00:45:51,969 --> 00:45:57,143
So imagine; the people of Egypt surrounding this stadium or this battlefield

637
00:45:57,430 --> 00:46:02,453
and all of them were afraid and terrified when they saw; what the magician's have done?

638
00:46:02,540 --> 00:46:04,400
What do you think the response of Musa(موسى) would be?

639
00:46:04,533 --> 00:46:05,940
And he is with them in the field.

640
00:46:07,140 --> 00:46:10,382
Remember; what happened before with Musa(موسى) when his stick started moving?

641
00:46:10,816 --> 00:46:11,562
What happened?

642
00:46:11,896 --> 00:46:13,589
فَوَلَّىٰ مُدْبِرًا وَلَمْ يُعَقِّبْ ۚ

643
00:46:14,249 --> 00:46:16,196
He ran away and he did not look back.

644
00:46:16,502 --> 00:46:18,296
And it was one stick.

645
00:46:19,039 --> 00:46:25,813
But now, look at the response of Musa(موسى);  seventy magicians or 15,000; throwing their sticks and their ropes;

646
00:46:26,906 --> 00:46:28,988
All the people around them are terrified.

647
00:46:29,282 --> 00:46:30,328
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

648
00:46:30,358 --> 00:46:32,615
فَأَوْجَسَ فِى نَفْسِهِۦ خِيفَةً مُّوسَىٰ۝

649
00:46:33,030 --> 00:46:34,655
Musa(موسى) conceived fear.

650
00:46:35,162 --> 00:46:35,735
Where?

651
00:46:35,968 --> 00:46:36,663
In his heart.

652
00:46:37,549 --> 00:46:44,356
But it did not show on his reaction; It did not show on his action; It did not show at all on Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى).

653
00:46:44,570 --> 00:46:47,572
It remained the natural human response in the heart.

654
00:46:48,418 --> 00:46:49,952
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى then said;

655
00:46:50,372 --> 00:46:56,035
قُلْنَا لَا تَخَفْ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلْأَعْلَىٰ۝

656
00:46:56,409 --> 00:46:59,135
Fear not, surely you will have the upper hand.

657
00:46:59,735 --> 00:47:03,829
Before he had fear in his heart and he acted upon it; He ran away and he didn't look back.

658
00:47:04,082 --> 00:47:07,536
Now, it was a natural human fear in the heart.

659
00:47:07,842 --> 00:47:10,793
But it's not affected Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) and that is what Eeman(ايمان) does.

660
00:47:11,693 --> 00:47:20,663
You still go through the natural human reactions or feelings of fear and doubt, all of these things that come to the heart,

661
00:47:20,863 --> 00:47:25,169
but the believer is able to suppress them and is able to eliminate them.

662
00:47:25,396 --> 00:47:27,689
And that is the difference between the believer and the non believer.

663
00:47:28,849 --> 00:47:34,406
So, Musa(موسى) here; he only concieved the little bit of fear in his heart but it did not affect him whatsoever.

664
00:47:34,686 --> 00:47:39,439
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى then gave Musa(موسى) Itma'nan(اطمئينان); he gave him tranquility.

665
00:47:39,606 --> 00:47:43,052
So that, small fear in the heart was eliminated and taken out of his heart.

666
00:47:43,846 --> 00:47:45,206
وَأَلْقِ مَا فِى يَمِينِكَ

667
00:47:45,312 --> 00:47:48,599
And throw that, which is in your right hand.

668
00:47:49,046 --> 00:47:53,812
Now; the 70 magicians have their sticks and their ropes shaking and moving.

669
00:47:54,285 --> 00:47:58,705
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى tells Musa(موسى) throw; what is in your right hand.

670
00:47:59,298 --> 00:48:00,922
تَلْقَفْ مَا صَنَعُوٓاْ ۖ

671
00:48:00,982 --> 00:48:04,052
It will eat up everything that they made.

672
00:48:04,217 --> 00:48:07,866
إِنَّمَا صَنَعُواْ كَيْدُ سَٰحِرٍۢ ۖ وَلَا يُفْلِحُ ٱلسَّاحِرُ حَيْثُ أَتَىٰ۝

673
00:48:08,012 --> 00:48:13,652
This is a plot of a magician and the plots of the magicians are not successful wherever they are.

674
00:48:14,186 --> 00:48:18,454
What is the difference between the stick of Musa(موسى) and the sticks of the magicians?

675
00:48:18,694 --> 00:48:25,033
The difference is that, the stick of Musa(موسى) had a living soul in it, that transformed the stick into a real snake.

676
00:48:25,540 --> 00:48:28,766
So it ate up all of their ropes.

677
00:48:29,213 --> 00:48:31,086
What was the response of the magicians?

678
00:48:31,580 --> 00:48:35,573
Who are the ones among all of these people, who are watching, who are the experts?

679
00:48:36,080 --> 00:48:38,153
Who are the ones who understand what's going on?

680
00:48:38,433 --> 00:48:39,480
The Magicians.

681
00:48:40,753 --> 00:48:43,522
Firaun(فرعون) is stubborn.

682
00:48:43,722 --> 00:48:44,708
He knows the truth.

683
00:48:45,255 --> 00:48:46,285
وَٱسْتَيْقَنَتْهَآ أَنفُسُهُمْ

684
00:48:46,315 --> 00:48:48,720
He knew the truth, but he doesn't want to believe.

685
00:48:49,234 --> 00:48:52,634
The people of Egypt surrounding are followers of Firaun(فرعون).

686
00:48:52,927 --> 00:48:55,247
Whatever Firaun(فرعون) says; we're going to follow him.

687
00:48:55,300 --> 00:48:56,720
فَٱسْتَخَفَّ قَوْمَهُۥ فَأَطَاعُوهُ ۚ

688
00:48:56,840 --> 00:48:58,896
He belittled his people, so they followed him.

689
00:48:59,143 --> 00:49:03,036
But the ones; who have understanding of the reality of the situation of the magicians;

690
00:49:03,263 --> 00:49:07,075
So, when they saw this; they understood that, this is not magic.

691
00:49:07,155 --> 00:49:08,455
We are the experts in magic.

692
00:49:08,649 --> 00:49:12,209
We know magic from A to Z.

693
00:49:12,282 --> 00:49:14,867
We know everything about it; This is not magic.

694
00:49:15,987 --> 00:49:19,839
This is not magic; this is a miracle from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

695
00:49:19,933 --> 00:49:21,953
So, when they saw that, the reaction was;

696
00:49:22,179 --> 00:49:23,813
فَأُلْقِىَ ٱلسَّحَرَةُ سُجَّدًا

697
00:49:24,006 --> 00:49:26,193
They made Sujood(سجود) to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and said;

698
00:49:26,253 --> 00:49:28,256
قَالُوٓاْ ءَامَنَّا بِرَبِّ هَٰرُونَ وَمُوسَىٰ

699
00:49:28,458 --> 00:49:30,531
We believed in the Lord of Haroon(هارون) and Musa(موسى).

700
00:49:31,385 --> 00:49:32,138
Firaun(فرعون) said;

701
00:49:32,247 --> 00:49:38,011
قَالَ ءَامَنتُمْ لَهُۥ قَبْلَ أَنْ ءَاذَنَ لَكُمْ ۖ

702
00:49:38,158 --> 00:49:39,078
He said;

703
00:49:39,805 --> 00:49:43,078
You believed in him before I gave you permission.

704
00:49:44,078 --> 00:49:46,715
Look at, how much control Firaun(فرعون) had over people.

705
00:49:46,775 --> 00:49:49,908
He even wants them to take permission from him, when they want to become Muslim.

706
00:49:50,802 --> 00:49:54,087
You have to get permission; a permit to believe in Musa(موسى).

707
00:49:54,514 --> 00:49:57,360
That is, how much control Firaun(فرعون) had, over the lives of people.

708
00:49:58,034 --> 00:50:02,682
قَالَ ءَامَنتُمْ لَهُۥ قَبْلَ أَنْ ءَاذَنَ لَكُمْ ۖ إِنَّهُۥ لَكَبِيرُكُمُ ٱلَّذِى عَلَّمَكُمُ ٱلسِّحْرَ

709
00:50:02,712 --> 00:50:08,631
Firaun(فرعون) said; He is your teacher; Musa(موسى) is your teacher, who taught you magic.

710
00:50:09,364 --> 00:50:10,891
And then he threatened them and said;

711
00:50:11,078 --> 00:50:23,275
فَلَأُقَطِّعَنَّ أَيْدِيَكُمْ وَأَرْجُلَكُم مِّنْ خِلَٰفٍۢ وَلَأُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ فِى جُذُوعِ ٱلنَّخْلِ

712
00:50:24,122 --> 00:50:36,228
وَلَأُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ فِى جُذُوعِ ٱلنَّخْلِ وَلَتَعْلَمُنَّ أَيُّنَآ أَشَدُّ عَذَابًا وَأَبْقَىٰ۝

713
00:50:36,970 --> 00:50:39,275
Verily, he is your chief, who taught to you magic.

714
00:50:39,507 --> 00:50:46,793
So, I will surely cut off your hands and your feet on opposite sides and I will surely crucify you on the trunks of palm trees.

715
00:50:47,247 --> 00:50:48,714
And then notice, what Firaun(فرعون) said;

716
00:50:49,174 --> 00:51:25,608
قَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ ءَامَنتُم بِهِۦ قَبْلَ أَنْ ءَاذَنَ لَكُمْ ۖ إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَمَكْرٌ مَّكَرْتُمُوهُ فِى ٱلْمَدِينَةِ لِتُخْرِجُواْ مِنْهَآ أَهْلَهَا ۖ فَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُونَ۝

717
00:51:25,854 --> 00:51:32,849
Firaun(فرعون) said; This is a conspiracy between you and Musa(موسى), which you have agreed about in the town before you came here;

718
00:51:33,509 --> 00:51:34,856
Look at this a blunt lie.

719
00:51:35,322 --> 00:51:36,807
He said; this is a conspiracy.

720
00:51:37,183 --> 00:51:39,683
You were conspiring with Musa(موسى) before you came here.

721
00:51:39,884 --> 00:51:48,750
In Surat-u-Shu'ara(سورةالشعراء); Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says that, when the magicians came and had their first meeting with Firaun(فرعون).

722
00:51:49,183 --> 00:51:51,310
The magicians were gathered from all over Egypt.

723
00:51:51,643 --> 00:51:55,900
When they were brought to Egypt and they had their first meeting with Firaun(فرعون), what did they say?

724
00:51:57,193 --> 00:52:00,773
What is the first thing the magician's told Firaun(فرعون), when they met with him?

725
00:52:01,173 --> 00:52:05,060
In the first meeting with Firaun(فرعون), they said;

726
00:52:05,220 --> 00:52:08,540
اَئِنَّ لَنَا لَأَجْرًا إِن كُنَّا نَحْنُ ٱلْغَٰلِبِينَ۝

727
00:52:09,073 --> 00:52:11,392
Are you going to reward us, if we win?

728
00:52:12,365 --> 00:52:14,650
So, they were in it for the money.

729
00:52:15,677 --> 00:52:18,924
That is why, they came; they want the reward.

730
00:52:19,164 --> 00:52:20,344
What did Firaun(فرعون) say?

731
00:52:20,670 --> 00:52:24,099
Yes, and you will also be close to me.

732
00:52:24,279 --> 00:52:28,779
So Firaun(فرعون), not only is going to give them wealth but he's going to give them power and position.

733
00:52:29,505 --> 00:52:32,598
They came for small worldly gain.

734
00:52:32,964 --> 00:52:35,505
And when they went into the field,

735
00:52:36,538 --> 00:52:44,617
it is said; Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says that, these magicians stood up and they threw their sticks and their ropes and they were chanting;

736
00:52:44,957 --> 00:52:47,594
بِعِزَّةِ فِرْعَوْنَ إِنَّا لَنَحْنُ ٱلْغَٰلِبُونَ۝

737
00:52:47,624 --> 00:52:50,027
بِعِزَّةِ فِرْعَوْنَ إِنَّا لَنَحْنُ ٱلْغَٰلِبُونَ۝

738
00:52:50,115 --> 00:52:52,300
In the name of Firaun(فرعون); We are going to win.

739
00:52:52,427 --> 00:52:54,314
In the name of Firaun(فرعون); We're going to win.

740
00:52:54,440 --> 00:52:56,193
And they were chanting these words.

741
00:52:57,440 --> 00:52:59,913
These magicians now became believers.

742
00:53:00,900 --> 00:53:04,006
And Firaun(فرعون) told them; I will kill you and I will crucify you.

743
00:53:04,066 --> 00:53:06,312
He will kill them in a cruel way.

744
00:53:06,486 --> 00:53:13,143
He's going to chop out; their arms and their legs and he's going to crucify them on palm trees.

745
00:53:14,329 --> 00:53:16,803
What was the response of the magicians now?

746
00:53:17,076 --> 00:53:26,381
قَالُواْ لَن نُّؤْثِرَكَ عَلَىٰ مَا جَآءَنَا مِنَ ٱلْبَيِّنَٰتِ وَٱلَّذِى فَطَرَنَا ۖ

747
00:53:26,901 --> 00:53:37,367
فَٱقْضِ مَآ أَنتَ قَاضٍ ۖ إِنَّمَا تَقْضِى هَٰذِهِ ٱلْحَيَوٰةَ ٱلدُّنْيَآ۝

748
00:53:37,801 --> 00:53:43,645
They said; We prefer you not over the clear signs that have came to us and to him, Allah who created us.

749
00:53:43,675 --> 00:53:49,728
So decree whatever you desire to decree, for you can only decree regarding the life of this world.

750
00:53:49,921 --> 00:53:56,925
إِنَّآ ءَامَنَّا بِرَبِّنَا لِيَغْفِرَ لَنَا خَطَٰيَٰنَا وَمَآ أَكْرَهْتَنَا عَلَيْهِ مِنَ ٱلسِّحْرِ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ خَيْرٌ وَأَبْقَىٰٓ۝

751
00:53:57,078 --> 00:54:04,256
Verily, we have believed in our Lord that He may forgive us our faults and the magic to which you have compelled us to do.

752
00:54:04,410 --> 00:54:08,721
And Allah is better as regards reward in comparison to yours.

753
00:54:09,647 --> 00:54:11,423
The reward of Allah is better than yours.

754
00:54:12,350 --> 00:54:13,943
Look at, what Eeman(ايمان) does.

755
00:54:14,990 --> 00:54:21,552
The same people who came and were asking for money, are now saying;

756
00:54:22,125 --> 00:54:29,671
We are not only willing to give our wealth; We're willing to give our life for the sake of Allah because the reward of a Allah is better.

757
00:54:30,244 --> 00:54:32,017
That is what Eeman(ايمان) does.

758
00:54:33,638 --> 00:54:38,891
And if our Eeman(ايمان) is not carrying us to that level than that means, our Eeman(ايمان) is very weak.

759
00:54:39,798 --> 00:54:45,757
Because  with the magicians; their Eeman(ايمان) transformed them from people who came to beg from Firaun(فرعون);

760
00:54:45,951 --> 00:54:49,571
to people who are willing to give their lives in the sake of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

761
00:54:51,017 --> 00:54:52,010
That is Eeman(ايمان).

762
00:54:52,610 --> 00:54:56,357
If our Eeman(ايمان) is not transforming us in that way, then we have a problem with our Eeman(ايمان).

763
00:54:56,437 --> 00:55:02,802
If we're not willing to give in the sake of Allah and to provide and to sacrifice, what Eeman(ايمان) do we have?

764
00:55:02,949 --> 00:55:04,055
Because the Deen(دِيْن) is;

765
00:55:04,085 --> 00:55:04,622
تضحية

766
00:55:04,658 --> 00:55:05,595
It's to sacrifice.

767
00:55:06,649 --> 00:55:08,883
And they died on Eeman(ايمان) and they were Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء).

768
00:55:09,577 --> 00:55:10,677
They died in the sake of Allah.

769
00:55:10,730 --> 00:55:16,649
These magicians, who were committing one of the major crimes and sins; magic, Eeman(ايمان) transformed them.

770
00:55:16,679 --> 00:55:20,409
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى accepts the Tawbah(توبة) of anyone and then they became Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) in the end.

771
00:55:21,389 --> 00:55:25,558
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْتسليما كثيرا

